veyard from the battlefield, if Bridge from Below is in your graveyard, create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token.\\nWhen a creature is put into an opponent's graveyard from the battlefield, if Bridge from Below is in your graveyard, exile Bridge from Below.", 'White spells you cast cost {1} less to cast.\\nBlue spells you cast cost {1} less to cast.\\nSpells your opponents cast cost {1} more to cast.', 'You gain 10 life. Then if you have more life than an opponent, create a 5/5 white Giant Warrior creature token.', 'You may choose not to untap Vedalken Shackles during your untap step.\\n{2}, {T}: Gain control of target creature with power less than or equal to the number of Islands you control for as long as Vedalken Shackles remains tapped.', '[+1]: Create a 1/1 white Soldier creature token.\\n[+1]: Target creature gets +3/+3 and gains flying until end of turn.\\n[−8]: You get an emblem with "Artifacts, creatures, enchantments, and lands you control have indestructible."', '[+1]: Creatures you control get +1/+1 and gain haste until end of turn.\\n[−2]: Gain control of target creature until end of turn. Untap that creature. It gains haste until end of turn.\\n[−6]: Create five 4/4 red Dragon creature tokens with flying.', "{1}{B}, {T}, Sacrifice Executioner's Capsule: Destroy target nonblack creature.", '{1}{G}, Sacrifice Hana Kami: Return target Arcane card from your graveyard to your hand.', '{1}{R}, Remove a time counter from a permanent you control or suspended card you own: Rift Elemental gets +2/+0 until end of turn.', '{1}{W}: Return target artifact card with mana value 1 or less from your graveyard to your hand.', "{2}, Exile a nonland card from your hand: Put four time counters on the exiled card. If it doesn't have suspend, it gains suspend. (At the beginning of your upkeep, remove a time counter from that card. When the last is removed, you may cast it without paying its mana cost. If it's a creature, it has haste.)", "{2}{W}, {T}, Sacrifice Dispeller's Capsule: Destroy target artifact or enchantment.", '{4}, {T}: Search your library for a Rebel permanent card with mana value 3 or less, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', '{B}, Sacrifice a Goblin: Facevaulter gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', '{B}, {T}: Tap target creature.', '{R/W}: Figure of Destiny becomes a Kithkin Spirit with base power and toughness 2/2.\\n{R/W}{R/W}{R/W}: If Figure of Destiny is a Spirit, it becomes a Kithkin Spirit Warrior with base power and toughness 4/4.\\n{R/W}{R/W}{R/W}{R/W}{R/W}{R/W}: If Figure of Destiny is a Warrior, it becomes a Kithkin Spirit Warrior Avatar with base power and toughness 8/8, flying, and first strike.', "{R}, Return Grinning Ignus to its owner's hand: Add {C}{C}{R}. Activate only as a sorcery.", '{R}, Sacrifice Pyrite Spellbomb: It deals 2 damage to any target.\\n{1}, Sacrifice Pyrite Spellbomb: Draw a card.', '{T}, Sacrifice Terramorphic Expanse: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{T}, Sacrifice a Goblin: Tar Pitcher deals 2 damage to any target.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}: Blinkmoth Nexus becomes a 1/1 Blinkmoth artifact creature with flying until end of turn. It's still a land.\\n{1}, {T}: Target Blinkmoth creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}{U}, {T}: Put target artifact card from your graveyard on top of your library.', '{T}: Target creature gets -2/-0 until end of turn.', '{T}: Target player exiles a card from their graveyard.\\n{1}, Exile Relic of Progenitus: Exile all graveyards. Draw a card.', '{T}: Target player loses 1 life.\\n{4}, {T}: Search your library for a Rebel permanent card with mana value 3 or less, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', "{U}, Sacrifice Aether Spellbomb: Return target creature to its owner's hand.\\n{1}, Sacrifice Aether Spellbomb: Draw a card."]
flavor: ['"An ancient, powerful force has overtaken the valley. I sympathize for its former inhabitants, but I rejoice for the land itself."\\n—Olanti, Muraganda druid', '"And that\'s when it was discovered that boggarts have just half a brain."\\n—*The Book of Other Folk*', '"Aren\'t there boggarts enough in Lorwyn? Couldn\'t it turn into a sheep? Or a sunflower?"\\n—Olly of Goldmeadow', '"Auntie Grub had caught a goat, a bleating doe that still squirmed in her arms. At the same time, her warren decided to share with her a sensory greeting of hot tar . . . ."\\n—A tale of Auntie Grub', '"Beauty determines value, and we determine beauty."', '"Before the war, we prayed to Kataki to sharpen our swords and harden our armor. Without his blessing our weapons are all but useless against the kami hordes."\\n—Kenzo the Hardhearted', '"Beings of the rifts are not natural. No longer will these abominations tread upon the body of Gaea."', '"Ever seen a changeling fly into a lantern?"\\n—Calydd, kithkin farmer', '"Fire is the universal language."\\n—Jhoira, master artificer', '"Give me a sword and I\'ll kill a few enemies. But give me a hammer and a fiery forge, and I\'ll turn the tide of battle."', '"Give up these unnatural weapons, these scrolls. Heart and mind and fist are enough."\\n—Zyd, Kamahlite druid', '"His laugh, a bellowing, deathly din, slices through the heavens, making them bleed."\\n—*The Seer\'s Parables*', '"I crept up on him, quiet as a guttermouse. And then suddenly I found myself facedown in a latrine pit behind Tin Street Market."\\n—Sirislav, Dimir spy', '"I find its symmetry pleasing. It rids our world of offensive refuse while disposing of itself."\\n—Dolomarus, Proctor of the Clean', '"It contains the wisdom of generations of our people. We permit only a chosen few to don the raiment."\\n—Imran, Viridian elder', '"It puts an end to what ails you."\\n—Jeorg, Valla battlemaster', '"It was vast, a great sheet of soaring wings, and equally silent. It caught us unawares and blocked our view of the kithkin stronghold."\\n—Grensch, merrow cutthroat', '"It\'s difficult to heal a rift after it begins wandering about on its own."\\n—Teferi', '"Know one part of the name, obsession begins. Know two parts, paranoia sets in. Know three parts, madness descends. Know all, and only the kami know what will become of you."\\n—Lady Azami', '"Knowledge of Bant\'s landscape and ruins is a weapon that the invaders can\'t comprehend."\\n—Elspeth', '"Master the chaotic forces of nature, and you shall master magic."\\n—Yare-Tiva, warden of Gramur forest', '"Melt that which was never frozen."\\n—Spellbomb inscription', '"Memnarch or the vedalken salvage most of the large machines, leaving us only scraps. Scraps are enough."', '"No matter how strong, an unarmed fighter is no more than a fool."', '"Rage is not the answer. Rage followed by fitting vengeance is the answer."\\n—Ajani', '"Release that which was never caged."\\n—Spellbomb inscription', '"Sages who take the time to verify their sources are rewarded for their diligence."\\n—Jhoira, to Teferi', '"She spoke of mystery and portent, of such unfathomable things that my mind screamed for pity."\\n—*The Seer\'s Parables*', '"Some goblins are expendable. Some are impossible to get rid of. But he\'s both—at the same time!"\\n—Starke', '"Take care what you offer the ignus. Food, perhaps. Coins. But nothing flammable!"\\n—Stovic, village eccentric', '"The jeweler, the potter, the smith . . . They all imbue a bit of their souls into their creations. The kami destroy that crafted mortal shell and absorb the soul within."\\n—Noboru, master kitemaker', '"The land grows only where the kami will it."\\n—Dosan the Falling Leaf', '"The landscape shimmered and I felt a chill breeze. When my vision cleared, I found myself alone among the corpses of my fallen friends."\\n—Journal found in Numai', '"The noble work of our order is to infuse all life on Esper with etherium. Our goal will be reached more rapidly if new life is . . . suppressed."', '"The soul is only as eternal as I say it is."\\n—Sharuum the Hegemon', '"There are all kinds of strengths, but if you have strength of soul, the others will follow."\\n—Galanda Feudkiller', '"There is much to learn here, but few can endure the ringing of the spires."\\n—Nulakam the Archivist', '"They\'d pour out of the warrens to make war (and to make room for the littering matrons)."\\n—*Sarpadian Empires, vol. IV*', '"Tie a mouse under a bridge, and your cabbages will triple in size."\\n—Kithkin superstition', '"To truly know something, you must become it. The trick is to not lose yourself in the process."', '"What do they need all this stuff for? They\'re dead. We\'re alive. Simple enough."', 'A fight put off forever is already won.', 'A single lie unleashes a tide of disbelief.', 'A single seed unleashes a flurry of growth.', "Accept one favor from an ouphe, and you're doomed to accept another.", 'Among the solitude-loving giantkind, teamwork is unusual. But he appreciates hearing the occasional "Swing down and to your left."', 'An empty canvas holds infinite possibilities.', "Arc mages aren't known for their patience.", 'As the dawns break, the manta soars.', 'As their supplies of etherium dwindled, mechanists sent gargoyles farther and farther afield in search of salvage.', 'At first, vedalken observers thought blinkmoths naturally avoided certain places. Then they realized those places were frogmite feeding grounds.', 'At night, the faeries steal dreamstuff for their queen. At daybreak, countless creatures wake weak and hollow.', 'Blood, bone, and sinew are magnified, as is the rage that drives them. The brain, however, remains unchanged—a little bean, swinging by a strand in a cavernous, raving head.', 'Boggarts constantly strive to outdo each other with the things they bring back to the warren, each hoping the exploit will become as well-known as those of Auntie Grub.', "Boggarts get so excited when they find something new to smash that they really don't notice who gets underfoot.", 'Death is only the beginning of the end.', 'During the collision of the shards, entire ways of life disappeared without a trace.', 'Each spell is an intricate tapestry, and Kira is the great unraveler.', 'Elves believe the hydra-god Progenitus sleeps beneath Naya, feeding on forgotten magics.', "Every culture has its unlucky numbers. In a city where you're either alone, in a crowd, or being stabbed in the back, two is the worst number of all.", 'Five-toed grave\\n—Kithkin phrase meaning "a giant\'s footprint"', 'From trinket to trauma.', 'Greatness, at any cost.', 'Ground into the footprints of the ravaging herd were clumps of salt from Benalia, moss from Llanowar, dust from Hurloon, and ash from as far as Urborg.', 'Growth has no limits.', 'He cares not for the disasters his storm brings as long as his path ahead is clear.', 'He loved his cities in the clouds. When he traveled to the lands below, he brought many reminders of his home.', 'He remembers a past of light and healing. But he lives the bitter present—parching salt, scouring wind, and the withering heat of the desert.', 'Heavy light flooded across the landscape, cloaking everything in deep crimson.', 'Held aloft by metabolized magic, trygons are ravenous for sources of mystic fuel.', 'In life, it was a fetid, disease-ridden thing. In death, not much changed.', 'It drifts through the streets as a breeze of collective sighs, wilting the bustle with dreams and heavy eyelids.', 'It grew in lands lit by pride and watered by tears.', 'It plucks away memories like choice bits of carrion.', 'It was created by the Iquati as a living memory—one that objects to being forgotten.', 'Its secrets once wrought the greatest artifice ever known. Now crabs loot the rubble to decorate their shells.', 'Its wings disturb more than air.', 'Jund feasts on the unprepared.', 'Leeches never tire of feeding.', 'Like being trapped in a perpetual sneeze, faerie-dust poisoning is both exhilarating and agonizing.', 'Mages of Esper measure their wealth and status by the number of servants in their retinues.', 'Mages often seek to emulate the powerful relics lost to time and apocalypse.', "Man's best fungus.", 'Mephidross gives up treasure easily . . . as long as you take its place.', 'Most myr monitor other species. Some myr monitor other myr.', 'One croaked sermon spreads propaganda and plague.', 'One part cunning, one part wise, and many, many parts demented.', "She doesn't escort the dead to the afterlife, but instead raises them to fight and die again.", 'She follows the old tributaries built when merrows still shaped the tides.', "She remembers every word spoken, from the hero's oath to the baby's cry.", 'Some kami attacks during the war were rife with trickery, subterfuge, and subtlety, draining hope and pride from the mortal world. Other attacks were a lot more straightforward.', 'Some who scouted new lands chose to stay.', 'Sometimes a curious giant singles out a "little one" to follow for a few days, never realizing the effect it will have on the little one\'s life.', 'Take two steps north into the unsettled future, south into the unquiet past, east into the present day, or west into the great unknown.', 'Takenuma was filled with a chorus of moans, shrieks, and wails. Some came from the living, some from the dying, and some, most horribly, from the dead.', "Tangling vines, fetid murk, paralyzing poisons, and crawling dead. The swamp is nature's trap waiting to be exploited by unnatural minds.", 'The Arbiter is a conduit of justice, a will so disciplined that it dispenses justice without ego or remorse.', 'The Izzet learn something from every lesson they teach.', 'The Soul of the World has returned.', 'The barbarians of Jund believe the bottomless tar pits extend forever into other, darker worlds.', "The fae know when they're not wanted. That's precisely why they show up.", 'The fall of the evening star never heralds a gentle dawn.', 'The giant was felt a few seconds before he was seen.', "The giants believe the fossils they find in Lorwyn's rocky heights are dreams frozen in time, and they treasure them.", 'The greatest masters of the craft abandon tools altogether, shaping metal with hand and mind alone.', 'The lamps on Wyndmoor Street snuff themselves at midnight and refuse to relight, afraid to illuminate what lies in the darkness.', 'The line between dream and death is gauzy and fragile. She leads those too near it from one side to the other.', "The more metal it digests, the more its jelly will fetch on the alchemists' market.", 'The more the scarier.', 'The paradise of Amrou Haven had become a field of cinders. Its people struggled to survive, hoping to see visions of its past in the strange storms that quickly passed.', 'The parts are as strong as the whole.', 'The people of Amrou were scattered by war and driven into hiding. Scouts maintain the beacon fires that signal "return" and "home."', "The swarm's million wings stir the foulest of breezes.", 'There is always a moment of trepidation before opening a message capsule, for fear of the judgment that might be contained within.', 'They seek out living trees to glean age-old secrets from sap and wood.', 'Those who expect betrayal at every turn are seldom disappointed.', 'Those who survive the test bear a mark of power anyone can recognize.', 'Today it flies with the flock. Tomorrow it may wake to find them gone, its body in an unfamiliar form.', "What doesn't grow, dies. And what dies grows the tarmogoyf.", 'When a changeling adopts a form no other changeling has taken, a rune appears in the caverns of Velis Vel to mark the event.', 'When it snared a passing cockatrice, its own soul darkly doubled.', 'When the School of the Unseen fell, so many magical treasures lay abandoned that no amount of death could deter the stream of thieves and desperate scholars.']
artist: ['Adam Paquette', 'Adam Rex', 'Aleksi Briclot', 'Anthony Francisco', 'Anthony S. Waters', 'Arnie Swekel', 'Brandon Kitkouski', 'Brian Despain', 'Carl Critchlow', 'Chippy', 'Chris Rahn', 'Christopher Moeller', 'Chuck Lukacs', 'Clint Cearley', 'Cyril Van Der Haegen', 'D. Alexander Gregory', 'Daarken', 'Dan Frazier', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Dan Seagrave', 'Daniel Ljunggren', 'Daren Bader', 'Darrell Riche', 'Dave Allsop', 'Donato Giancola', 'Doug Chaffee', 'Eric Fortune', 'Franz Vohwinkel', 'Fred Fields', 'Glen Angus', 'Greg Hildebrandt', 'Greg Staples', 'Heather Hudson', 'Hideaki Takamura', 'Hiro Izawa', 'Howard Lyon', 'Ittoku', 'Izzy', 'Jack Wang', 'Jaime Jones', 'James Kei', 'James Paick', 'Janine Johnston', 'Jason Chan', 'Jasper Sandner', 'Jean-Sébastien Rossbach', 'Jeff Easley', 'Jeremy Enecio', 'Jeremy Jarvis', 'Jesper Ejsing', 'Jim Murray', 'Jim Nelson', 'Jim Pavelec', 'John Avon', 'Jon Foster', 'Jung Park', 'Karl Kopinski', 'Kev Walker', 'Lars Grant-West', 'Luca Zontini', 'Marco Nelor', 'Mark Poole', 'Mark Tedin', 'Mark Zug', 'Martina Pilcerova', 'Matt Cavotta', 'Matt Stewart', 'Matt Thompson', 'Michael Bruinsma', 'Michael Komarck', 'Michael Phillippi', 'Michael Sutfin', 'Mike Dringenberg', 'Nils Hamm', 'Nottsuo', 'Omar Rayyan', 'Pete Venters', 'Quinton Hoover', 'Ralph Horsley', 'Randy Gallegos', 'Raymond Swanland', 'Rebecca Guay', 'Rob Alexander', 'Ron Spears', 'Ron Spencer', 'Ryan Barger', 'Sam Burley', 'Scott Altmann', 'Scott M. Fischer', 'Shelly Wan', 'Shishizaru', 'Stephen Tappin', 'Steve Prescott', 'Steven Belledin', 'Svetlin Velinov', 'Terese Nielsen', 'Thomas M. Baxa', 'Todd Lockwood', 'Trevor Claxton', 'Trevor Hairsine', 'Tsutomu Kawade', 'Vance Kovacs', 'Volkan Baǵa', 'Warren Mahy', 'Wayne England', 'Wayne Reynolds', 'William Simpson', 'Zack Stella', 'Zoltan Boros & Gabor Szikszai', 'rk post']
